  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Palme Center Programme in Albania  2019-2022</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Palme Center Programme in Albania 2019-2022 - Palme Center Programme in Albania 2019-2021</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Olof Palme International Center/OPC has applied for a new phase of its programme in Albania 2018-2021 with a budget of 15,6 MSEK out of which 61% is forwarded to Albanian partner organisations.  The main objective of the programme is to strengthen the capacity and legitimacy of civil society organisations and support activities that ensure the participatory nature of political and social processes and accountability of duty bearers. The intervention focuses on two thematic areas: 1) Citizens participation and 2) Socio/economic/labour rights. The number of partners in the first area is reduced compared to previous programmes and priority is given to joint actions by partners targeting primarily youth and women. The second area- labour rights-  is expanded compared to the previous programme and the assessment is that that OPC has made strategic choices in terms of what sectors to prioritise (Fashion industry, extracting industry and Call centres) and what would be the approaches for enhancing the cooperation between trade unions and civil society organisations.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Olof Pame International Center/OPC har ans&#xf6;kt om nytt st&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r deras Albanienprogram 2018-2021 med en budget p&#xe5; 15.6 MSEK d&#xe4;r 61% av medlen &#xe4;r t&#xe4;nkt att f&#xf6;rmedlas vidare till albanska partnerorganisationer. St&#xf6;det syftar till att st&#xe4;rka civilsamh&#xe4;llsorganisationers kapacitet och legitimitet samt att st&#xf6;dja partners aktiviteter f&#xf6;r deltagande i olika sociala och politiska processer och att bl a fr&#xe4;mja ansvarsutkr&#xe4;vande. Insatsen har tv&#xe5; tematiska omr&#xe5;den: 1) Medborgardeltagande och 2) Sociala och ekonomiska r&#xe4;ttigheter samt arbetstagares r&#xe4;ttigheter. Antalet partners inom det f&#xf6;rsta omr&#xe5;det har minskats ned och prioritet ges till partners som s&#xe4;rskilt arbetar med unga och kvinnor. Det andra omr&#xe5;det har utvidgats j&#xe4;mf&#xf6;rt med tidigare st&#xf6;d och Sida bed&#xf6;mer att OPC har gjort strategiska val avseende vilka sektorer som ska f&#xe5; st&#xf6;d (mode- och utvinningsindustrierna samt Call centres) och den valda ansatsen och metodiken f&#xf6;r att st&#xe4;rka samarbetet mellan fackliga organisationer och civilsamh&#xe4;llet.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the intervention is strengthening the role of civil society focusing on two main thematic areas: 1. citizen participation in decision-making and 2. socio-economic and labour rights. 
The expected results of the intervention are: 1) Partner organisations expand the popular base, create networks for joint actions and have capacities to monitor the implementation of political decisions and influence policy agenda. 2) Citizens and citizens groups are empowered, organised, participate and influence in decision making and demand transparency and accountability from duty bearers. 3) Strengthened capacity of employees, trade unions and other CSOs working for increased access to decent work and the rights of workers.</narrative>
  </description>
